                <pb facs="0538" n="1292" xml:id="pg1292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Sp1/15</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-29T22:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1917, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 30, 1 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>648. The King this afternoon signed the following Royal decree: <list>
                        <item>Article 1. Submarines of every class of all belligerent nations are
                            prohibited in Spanish jurisdictional waters and entrance into Spanish
                            ports.</item>
                        <item>Art. 2. All submarines included in the previous article which enter
                            Spanish jurisdiction for whatsoever reason shall be interned until the
                            close of the war.</item>
                        <item>Art. 3. Neutral submarines entering Spanish jurisdictional waters must
                            navigate on the surface and show plainly the national flag.</item>
                        <item>Art. 4. The Royal decree of November 23, 1914, shall remain in force
                            in so far as it is not modified by the present decree.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
